  == Master Bank — Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 1.* A — after to the bare infinitive is required: to bring. Brings is finite, brought is past, and bringing is the present participle.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 2.* C — one dependent clause (when the bell rang) plus one independent clause makes it complex. A is simple; B and D are compound.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 3.* B — married to is the fixed pair. With, by and the bare construction are translations rather than English collocations.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 4.* B — scissors is a paired object and always plural, so are. Is, was and has been are singular forms.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 5.* B — diligent means showing steady effort. Lazy is its opposite, and intelligent and wealthy name other qualities.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 6.* B — prudent means showing good judgement. Reckless is its opposite, and wealth and silence are unrelated.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 1.* B — deny takes a gerund: denied breaking. To break would follow refuse or agree, and break and broke are finite forms that cannot follow denied.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 2.* B — no sooner takes had and inverts with the subject: no sooner had he arrived. Did and has do not form the past perfect, and was cannot take arrived.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 3.* A — a permanent truth keeps its present tense even after a past reporting verb, so is. Was would make the earth's shape a past fact, and the other two change the sense.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    *Chapter 4.* B — concise means saying much in few words. Lengthy is its opposite, and confusing and polite are unrelated.
